\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces Bayesian model comparison for a mock detection at $f_{\rm  NL}= -4.375$ with $\sigma = 0.7$ and a delta-function bounce prior. SSFSR = standard single-field slow-roll inflation. The range 8--11 reflects different GR treatment scenarios (Table~\ref {tab:gr}). Broadening the bounce prior to a Gaussian with $\sigma _{\rm  theory} = 1.0$ reduces these to $\sim 8$--17 (abstract headline).}}{7}{table.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:bayes}{{II}{7}{Bayesian model comparison for a mock detection at $\fnl = -4.375$ with $\sigma = 0.7$ and a delta-function bounce prior. SSFSR = standard single-field slow-roll inflation. The range 8--11 reflects different GR treatment scenarios (Table~\ref {tab:gr}). Broadening the bounce prior to a Gaussian with $\sigma _{\rm theory} = 1.0$ reduces these to $\sim 8$--17 (abstract headline)}{table.2}{}}
